{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 560,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This episode was sponsored by KiwiCo"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 2920,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More about them at the end of the show"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 6600,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Until recently, half the universe was missing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 10200,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or hidden or just... undetected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12640,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And no, I'm not talking about dark matter or dark energy,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15520,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which make up 27 and 68 percent of our universe, respectively."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19520,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, I'm talking about normal ordinary matter"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 22480,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which makes up you and me and the planets and stars and nebulae,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 26320,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and basically everything you can see."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 29320,
    "dDurationMs": 5320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since most of this stuff is made of protons and neutrons, which are forms of baryons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34640,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "this has been known as the missing baryon problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38360,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We expect the universe to be made up of 5 percent baryonic matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 42800,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But when we go looking, we only find 2.5 percent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 47560,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, the first question you're probably asking is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 50080,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "\"Why should we expect the universe to be 5 percent ordinary baryonic matter in the first place?\""
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 55840,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The answer is because, with that density,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 58440,
    "dDurationMs": 6000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can explain the relative abundances of different elements that we observe in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 64440,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Specifically, the ratio of deuterium to hydrogen to helium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 69600,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the beginning, like right after the Big Bang,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 72920,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there were all of these neutrons and protons whizzing around."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75760,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was incredibly hot, and there was tons of radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 78720,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The universe was radiation dominated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 81080,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, as the universe expanded, it cooled to the point where protons and neutrons could start fusing together."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 88000,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A particularly stable nucleus to form would be helium-4,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91600,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "made of two neutrons and two protons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 94040,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem was, to form helium-4, you first have to form deuterium, one proton and one neutron."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100720,
    "dDurationMs": 6340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And, this is a less stable nucleus. And as quickly as it formed, it would get smashed apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 107120,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But, by about 10 seconds after the big bang,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 109760,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the universe had cooled sufficiently that deuterium could form."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 113920,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And as soon as it did, it would rapidly fuse into helium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 117640,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The rate at which this happened depended on the density of matter in the early universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 122680,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The higher the density - the faster this fusion could occur."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 126720,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Then, by 20 minutes after the Big Bang,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129080,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the temperature had dropped low enough that fusion could no longer occur."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 133600,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, at this point, the elemental abundances were locked in."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 137320,
    "dDurationMs": 2840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Like a snapshot of this moment."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140160,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There were 75% hydrogen and 25% helium, by mass."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144200,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Which is basically still what we observe in the universe today."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 148000,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Of the hydrogen nuclei,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149680,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "26 out of every million were deuterium."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 156200,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's amazing about deuterium is that it's stable - it doesn't decay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 160760,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there are no known processes that can produce it in significant quantities since the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166240,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that means, virtually all the deuterium in the universe today,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 169520,
    "dDurationMs": 4800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "including the one out of every 6000 hydrogen atoms in tap water"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 174320,
    "dDurationMs": 5440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "was created not in stars but in the first 20 minutes after the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180920,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When we look deep into space,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 183960,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the oldest light we can see is the Cosmic Microwave Background Radiation."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 188520,
    "dDurationMs": 5160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The afterglow of the big bang which has been traveling through the universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193680,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "unimpeded since about 400,000 years after the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198160,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so we can literally count up those photons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 200600,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and work out the density of radiation right after the Big Bang."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 205960,
    "dDurationMs": 5480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And using the value of 26 deuterium nuclei per million hydrogen nuclei,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 211440,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, we can work out the ratio of baryonic matter to photons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 215640,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that is how we work out that there should be about five percent baryonic matter in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221960,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in the late 1990s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 223480,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "scientists went looking for all this baryonic matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 227000,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It was a census of sorts."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229600,
    "dDurationMs": 6920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They added up all of the planets and stars and black holes, galaxies, dust clouds, gas,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 236520,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "basically everything you can see or infer exists using a telescope."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 242080,
    "dDurationMs": 6840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what they found is that everything that I normally think of as the actual stuff in our universe,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 248920,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it only makes up barely 20 percent of all the baryonic matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 254160,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So where is the rest?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257120,
    "dDurationMs": 6320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, not all ordinary matter is glowing brightly or is illuminated by nearby stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 263440,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's not dark matter but it is ordinary matter that is just in darkness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269000,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so if you want to find those baryons,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271880,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "well, one way is to use a backlight"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 275200,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "-- a bright source of light very far away,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278000,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that also means in the very early universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 281160,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And quasars are the perfect backlight."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 284480,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Their luminosity can be thousands of times that of whole galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289680,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The light comes from the accretion disk of a supermassive black hole"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 293880,
    "dDurationMs": 1960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at the center of an early galaxy"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 295840,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as it engulfs all this matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 299080,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And since it is so distant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 300920,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the light we receive from quasars is heavily redshifted."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 304840,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, the light emitted when a hydrogen atom"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 307200,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "goes from its first excited state to its ground state,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309800,
    "dDurationMs": 1840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the Lyman-alpha transition,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 311640,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it produces ultraviolet light of around 121.6 nanometers in a lab."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317360,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But from a quasar it can be observed as a peak in their spectrum"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 321640,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "at over 560 nanometers -- that is yellow light."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326880,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What's fascinating is if you look to the left of this peak"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330240,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you see many little dips."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 332560,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are absorption lines created by neutral hydrogen atoms"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336680,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that lie along our line of sight with the quasar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339880,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When light from the quasar reaches neutral hydrogen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 343400,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the photons that can excite the electrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 345840,
    "dDurationMs": 3440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from the ground state to the first excited state are absorbed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349280,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the same Lyman-alpha transition,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 352360,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but since these patches of hydrogen gas are closer to us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355720,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are less redshifted"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 358200,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the notches they make in the spectrum are at shorter and shorter wavelengths the closer the gas is to us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366080,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This has been described as the Lyman-alpha forest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370880,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's like a one-dimensional map"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373240,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that shows us where and how much neutral hydrogen gas"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 377320,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "lies along the line connecting us to the quasar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383440,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Adding all of that neutral hydrogen gas into our baryon budget"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386800,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "brings us almost to 50 percent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 390160,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So where is the other half of the baryons?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393680,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, computer simulations of the entire universe suggested"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397440,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they are out there just in between the galaxies in these sheets or filaments"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403640,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they're very spread out -- just one to ten particles per cubic meter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 408920,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Plus, these particles are ionized so they don't absorb the light like the neutral hydrogen gas."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 414960,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And they're in a temperature range between about 100,000 and 10 million Kelvin,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 420000,
    "dDurationMs": 3360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "a range astronomers like to refer to as warm-hot,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423360,
    "dDurationMs": 6040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so this is known as the warm-hot intergalactic medium or WHIM for short."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429400,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But finding the WHIM has been a real challenge"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 432640,
    "dDurationMs": 2160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they're ionized, because of their temperature,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 434800,
    "dDurationMs": 5560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they only emit or absorb in the high energy UV or low energy X-rays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440560,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, some people have used very sophisticated techniques to try to find the WHIM"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 445560,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but then recently a naturally occurring physical phenomenon"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 449280,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "allowed us to find all of the missing baryons."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 452400,
    "dDurationMs": 1240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's find out how."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 454760,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "First we need to talk lightning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 457720,
    "dDurationMs": 2080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I promise this is related."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 459800,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay so did you know that it's possible to detect lightning from the other side of the earth?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 465600,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is because lightning produces a flash of electromagnetic radiation in all parts of the spectrum."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471400,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean we see the white light but there's also broad spectrum radio waves which are released"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477020,
    "dDurationMs": 4060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if you were nearby you could detect those as a pulse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 481080,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the very low frequency radio waves can actually travel up and out of the atmosphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486680,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they get guided along the Earth's magnetic field lines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490200,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out several radii from the Earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492680,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then back down where they can be detected in the other hemisphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496720,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Except if they're detected there they don't come in as a single pulse,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 501440,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "instead they are spread out as a whistler."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 504720,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now if you play these radio waves through a speaker"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 507120,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we can actually hear them, so listen to this."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514920,
    "dDurationMs": 2360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You hear that descending tone"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517280,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that sounds like a sci-fi laser gun?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 519920,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, that is lightning on the other side of the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523760,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So what's happening here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525560,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, as the radio waves travel through the earth's magnetosphere"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529480,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they encounter free electrons, which slows them down"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533400,
    "dDurationMs": 5040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and more for the lower frequency waves: this is dispersion."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 538440,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just as a prism separates white light into its component colors"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 542280,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the plasma in the magnetosphere separates the radio waves into its component frequencies:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 547800,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "low frequencies are slowed down more than high frequencies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550920,
    "dDurationMs": 3520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so what started as a pulse ends up as a whistler."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 554440,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And the amount of dispersion tells you how many free electrons"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558440,
    "dDurationMs": 2600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that radio wave had to pass through to reach the detector."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 561960,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now just imagine we could do something very similar"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 564880,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to find all the ionized baryons in the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 568360,
    "dDurationMs": 7040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "All we would need is a bright flash of radio waves somewhere in the distant universe"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 575400,
    "dDurationMs": 6800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as if on cue in 2007 astronomers found the first fast radio burst,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 582200,
    "dDurationMs": 6120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which is just what it sounds like: a very short-duration pulse of intense radio waves."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 588320,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And it came from the deep universe, from other galaxies."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 593120,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now, these pulses can be incredibly powerful,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 596040,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I'm talking billions or trillions of times as powerful as the sun,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 600360,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but they last for on order of a millisecond."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603960,
    "dDurationMs": 2120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We don't really know what creates them,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606080,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "though some people suspect that it's magnetars or neutron stars"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 610100,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or some sort of collision between these very powerful massive objects"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 614400,
    "dDurationMs": 2520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like black holes and neutron stars."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 616920,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But for our purposes all we need to know is that those flashes exist"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622760,
    "dDurationMs": 2760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that we can use them to look at their dispersion"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 625520,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and figure out how many ionized baryons are between us and the source."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629960,
    "dDurationMs": 3920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And this is exactly what one recent paper did in Nature:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 633880,
    "dDurationMs": 5280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they plotted out the dispersion measure of several of these fast radio bursts"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639160,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "versus the redshift of their host galaxy."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 642840,
    "dDurationMs": 5000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And what they found was, sure enough, the further out these fast radio bursts were"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647840,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the more dispersed their signal when it reached the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 651480,
    "dDurationMs": 2320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And in fact using their measurements"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they were able to estimate the total baryonic matter that is out there,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658680,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and that includes all the ionized particles in the WHIM,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 661640,
    "dDurationMs": 3000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they found that it was five percent."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 665400,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They found the missing baryons. Roughly 50 percent of them"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 669120,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are in that warm-hot intergalactic medium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672600,
    "dDurationMs": 3880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so this validates what we had been thinking the whole time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 677320,
    "dDurationMs": 3600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know, what surprised me in making this video was realizing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 680920,
    "dDurationMs": 2880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "just how little of the ordinary matter from the big bang"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 683800,
    "dDurationMs": 2280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "ended up in things like stars and galaxies,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 686080,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what I normally consider as the stuff of the universe."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689320,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, that's only like 10 or 20 percent of all the baryonic matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 693240,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So it turns out the formation of these interesting structures"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 696280,
    "dDurationMs": 2200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "is a really inefficient process."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 699040,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this finding is yet another triumph for science."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 702680,
    "dDurationMs": 4640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Those computer simulations run decades ago turned out largely to be correct"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 707320,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and so everyone involved should be congratulated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710360,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this also highlights for me the difference between scientists and non-scientists."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714680,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I feel like non-scientists like being right,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 717920,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they like when things turn out the way they were expecting,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 720640,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but scientists on the other hand, they want things to work out not the way they expected"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 726160,
    "dDurationMs": 2440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because that's the way we get clues into"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 728600,
    "dDurationMs": 2800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what new physics is still out there to be discovered."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732240,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I guess for now we'll have to be content with being right."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 740800,
    "dDurationMs": 2480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, this video was sponsored by kiwiko"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 743280,
    "dDurationMs": 3400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which i'm really excited about because i've been using their monthly crates"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 746680,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "since the beginning of the year with my four-year-old, he got it as a christmas present"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 751040,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I've got to say they have been a great resource for learning at home."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 754680,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each crate has super cool hands-on projects that are fun to make and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 759040,
    "dDurationMs": 6200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They expose kids to STEAM concepts: that's science technology engineering art and math"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 765240,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now each box includes all the supplies needed meaning no extra trips to the store"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 770000,
    "dDurationMs": 4360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and kiwico offers eight subscription lines for different age groups and topics"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 774360,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "they sent me some of the older age group crates to try out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 777840,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I had a lot of fun uh making this…… this is a planetarium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 782000,
    "dDurationMs": 4040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and something you might not know is kiwico is not only a subscription service"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 786040,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can browse their store and purchase individual projects or value packs for different ages"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 790880,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "no subscription required"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 792360,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so let's talk about why kiwico is so useful right now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 795640,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I mean anyone who has been at home with kids over the past few months"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 798800,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "knows just how important it is to get them engaged in something other than a screen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 803360,
    "dDurationMs": 2240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the summer brain drain happens every year"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 805600,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "but it is especially challenging right now with disruptions to school"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 809800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and online learning just not being as good as you know in in-person hands-on learning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814920,
    "dDurationMs": 4200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now what I know from my own experience is my son loves making kiwico projects with me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 820480,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "he has a lot of fun and doesn't even realize he's learning"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823200,
    "dDurationMs": 760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what do you see"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 823960,
    "dDurationMs": 1520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's a star!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 825480,
    "dDurationMs": 3120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You know one day we will talk about the missing baryons but for right now"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 828600,
    "dDurationMs": 3760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "these projects are a great way for us to connect and learn together"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 832360,
    "dDurationMs": 1040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so if you want to try it out"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833400,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "you can get 20% off everything in the kiwico store using code: veritasium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 837800,
    "dDurationMs": 4320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or go to kiwico.com/veritasium I'll put that link in the description"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 842120,
    "dDurationMs": 2400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so I really want to thank kiwiko for supporting me"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844520,
    "dDurationMs": 2000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I want to thank you for watching"
    } ]
  } ]
}
